        "type": "the-purpose",
        "title": "Untitled",
        "body": "This topic set explores NASA's profound contributions to the field of cosmology, specifically curated for an audience without a formal background in mathematics or science. The central goal is to move beyond complex equations and focus on the conceptual, historical, and technological narratives behind NASA's greatest missions. These topics examine the \"why\" and \"how\" of cosmic discovery—from the engineering marvels built to observe the universe to the way raw data is translated into inspiring images. This set is designed to be highly educational and challenging by focusing on the strategic questions, human ingenuity, and philosophical implications of NASA's quest to understand our universe's origins, evolution, and ultimate fate.",
        "line_number": 27,
