      "unordered": [
        {
          "text": "**The \"Technosignature\" Search:** How NASA and the SETI institute are developing strategies to search for signs of technology, not just life, elsewhere in the universe.",
          "indent_level": 1,
          "line_number": 92,
          "source": "topic-set-nasas-cosmological-quest-🆔20251106223911.md"
        },
        {
          "text": "**The Voyager's \"Pale Blue Dot\":** A more philosophical inquiry into the cultural and intellectual impact of NASA's probes (Voyager, Pioneer) leaving the solar system and looking back at Earth.",
          "indent_level": 1,
          "line_number": 97,
          "source": "topic-set-nasas-cosmological-quest-🆔20251106223911.md"
        },
        {
          "text": "**Planetary Science as a Cosmological Tool:** How studying the planets in our *own* solar system (e.g., the missions to Mars, Jupiter, and Saturn) helps NASA understand the general rules of planet formation throughout the cosmos.",
          "indent_level": 1,
          "line_number": 97,
          "source": "topic-set-nasas-cosmological-quest-🆔20251106223911.md"
        },
        {
          "text": "**Astrobiology and the \"Habitable Zone\":** The conceptual framework NASA uses to identify which distant exoplanets (planets around other stars) are the most likely candidates to harbor life, and how missions like Kepler and TESS conduct this census.",
          "indent_level": 1,
          "line_number": 106,
          "source": "topic-set-nasas-cosmological-quest-🆔20251106223911.md"
        }
      ]
